description:
Description of a target ISA, in `simd_ext/<isa>/<isa>_isa.json` (and `helpers_headers/registry_scalar_isa.json` for the scalar fallback). Adding a directory with this file and the native implementation files is enough to add an ISA ([Add an ISA](../../tutorials/add_isa.md)).

Checked when the file is loaded, in addition to the schema:

- `sub_isa` names an existing directory of `simd_ext/`;
- a negative factor in `sw_lmul` requires `sw_ldiv_type: sub_isa`, and only `-2` is supported;
- `sw_ldiv_type: sub_isa` requires `sub_isa`, and a `size` twice the size of `sub_isa`;
- `info_names` has at most one entry without `if`, in last position.

Top-level keys are sorted alphabetically (`json-structure` audit).
